 script="joy2key_sdl.py"

# Why: RetroPie's default joy2key mapping sends Space for button 1 and Esc for
# button 2, so on a Game Boy style layout 'B' does not cancel - 'X' does.
# Swapping the two codes makes A=OK (Enter) and B=Cancel (Esc).
#
# NOTE: /opt/retropie/admin/joy2key/joy2key is installed by RetroPie-Setup.
# Reinstalling the joy2key package reverts this. Re-apply with:
#   sudo patch -p0 -d /opt/retropie/admin/joy2key < joy2key-b-cancels.patch
